msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-make-content-addressed.md:46
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-make-content-addressed.md:48
msgid ""
"This command converts the closure of the store paths specified by "
"[_installables_](./nix.md#installables) to content-addressed form."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-make-content-addressed.md:51
msgid ""
"Nix store paths are usually _input-addressed_, meaning that the hash part of "
"the store path is computed from the contents of the derivation (i.e., the "
"build-time dependency graph). Input-addressed paths need to be signed by a "
"trusted key if you want to import them into a store, because we need to "
"trust that the contents of the path were actually built by the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-make-content-addressed.md:59
msgid ""
"By contrast, in a _content-addressed_ path, the hash part is computed from "
"the contents of the path. This allows the contents of the path to be "
"verified without any additional information such as signatures. This means "
"that a command like"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-make-content-addressed.md:64
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix build /nix/store/5skmmcb9svys5lj3kbsrjg7vf2irid63-hello-2.10 \\\n"
"    --substituters https://my-cache.example.org\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-make-content-addressed.md:69
msgid ""
"will succeed even if the binary cache `https://my-cache.example.org` doesn't "
"present any signatures."
msgstr ""

